  "provider_query": "Public Telegram web preview of the official Telegram channel",
  "answer": "The official Telegram channel is **@telegram** (Telegram News). Public posts are viewable on the web without an account via the `/s/` preview.\n\n1. **Channel preview feed** — https://t.me/s/telegram — public web view of the official channel (“The official Telegram on Telegram”).  \n2. **Channel link** — https://t.me/telegram — opens the channel in Telegram or the web preview.  \n3. **Example post preview** — https://t.me/s/telegram/81 — single-post web view (embed docs reference this style of link).  \n4. **Older page of the same feed** — https://t.me/s/telegram?before=461 — paginated public preview of earlier posts.  \n5. **Channels tour (official docs)** — https://telegram.org/tour/channels — states public channel contents are visible on the web (example format `t.me/s/…`) and points to the official @Telegram channel.  \n6. **Channels FAQ** — https://telegram.org/faq_channels — notes public channels use a `t.me/` username link (example: `t.me/telegram`).  \n7. **Post embed widget docs** — https://core.telegram.org/widgets/post — how public channel posts (opened via `t.me` links) can be embedded on the web.  \n8. **Deep links reference** — https://core.telegram.org/api/links — documents public username links such as `t.me/<username>` and message links `t.me/<username>/<id>`.",
